course: dictionary
lesson: 6430
title: Myrrh and context clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Myrrh is a noun, which means it names a thing. You may not know it, but the words around it give clues: «Wise men from the East brought gold, frankincense and myrrh.» Gold and frankincense are precious gifts, so myrrh must be something valuable that you could give.
explain: The sentence also says frankincense and myrrh are two sweet-smelling tree gums. A gum is a sticky substance that comes out of a tree, so the clues tell you what kind of thing myrrh is before you even look it up.
explain: Some words also carry a story. In a nativity play, myrrh is the «sad» gift, because it points to Jesus's death. The dictionary tells you what myrrh is; the story tells you why it matters to people.
fact: Myrrh is a bitter, sweet-smelling gum (resin) from a small thorny tree in Arabia and Africa.
fact: Myrrh is used in perfumes, medicines and incense.
fact: Myrrh was one of three gifts the wise men gave baby Jesus, with gold and frankincense.
fact: Christians see myrrh as a sign of Jesus's death, because myrrh was used to prepare bodies for burial.
fact: The Bible does not say how many wise men there were; it only tells us there were three gifts.
exercise: «Wise men from the East brought gold, frankincense and myrrh.» What is myrrh? | A hot spice that is eaten in curries | A soft cloth used for wrapping babies | *A sweet-smelling, bitter gum from a small thorny tree | A shiny metal, as valuable as gold
exercise: Myrrh was one of three gifts the wise men gave baby Jesus. Which two other gifts were given with it? | Books and honey | Silver and bread | Coins and cloth | *Gold and frankincense
exercise: «Saba was a kingdom rich from trading frankincense and myrrh.» What does this tell you about myrrh? | It was a kind of animal | *It was valuable, something people bought and sold | It was dangerous to touch | It only grew in gardens in England
test: Ancient Egyptians used myrrh when making what? | Kites | Pottery | *Mummies | Bread
test: Christians see myrrh as a sign of what? | A happy wedding | *Jesus's death | A harvest festival
exam: Which sentence best explains what myrrh is? | A happy song sung at Christmas | *A sweet-smelling, bitter gum from a small thorny tree | A bright gold coin from the Middle East | A thorny bush you can eat like fruit
